This project studies upper bounds on the irrationality exponent of Catalan's constant.

The determinant construction and its original irrationality proof are due to
OpenAI (2026). The design (58,9,3,5,3), the uniform nonvanishing and denominator
theorems, the 102-piece rank-deficiency profile, the trial sequences, and the
generic quadrature and energy lemmas used here come from Sean Litsey's
catalan-irrationality-measure repository, under Apache License 2.0.

Upstream repository: https://github.com/slitsey/catalan-irrationality-measure
Pinned revision: aa2a42f4f3835347ad46608779e22dd52c2dc7bf

certificates/rank_profile.json transcribes the wins532 data from
CatalanMeasure/GenD/Uniform/Bank532/Ledger532.lean. It does not replace the
upstream proof that these functions bound the prime-by-prime nullities.

certificates/trial_data.json transcribes the unchanged second-case P trial
from CatalanMeasure/GenD/D58/Cert590/Data.lean, Git blob
c401f993810de11834f6db6ce5eda4064be09021. Its source and data hashes are recorded
and verified by scripts/residual_certificate.py.

New code in scripts/ checks the new rational certificates and numerical
implications. These scripts are not Lean kernel checks of the complete proof.

See LICENSE for the Apache License 2.0.

The Lean dependency closure under Submission/ is copied from the pinned
upstream project, with imports of vendored roots prefixed by Submission.
The guarded compatibility patch in scripts/vendor_lean.py changes one proof
step in CatalanMeasure/GenD/Cert/Assembly.lean for Lean 4.34.1: an existing
Boolean equality hypothesis is used directly. No mathematical statement or
definition changes. The provenance manifest records this patch and both hashes.
The original upstream NOTICE is preserved in third_party/UPSTREAM_NOTICE.
New modules under Submission/Refinement/ and Submission/Improvement/ are
additions in this repository. The trusted CatalanStatement.lean is copied
unchanged from bigospeedrun/verifier.
